@prefix chorus: <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# =============================================================================
# #4045 — the nine products, in a file, on the IRIs the API serves.
#
# Until now every Product row (chorus:athena … chorus:werk, and spine minted
# 2026-09-01) existed ONLY in the live store: no deploy could reproduce them,
# and the #3603-era product-* rows this file used to hold were retired live but
# kept here, so the file described a graph that no longer existed. Same class of
# fix as #3838 (roles) and #4040 (pipelines): day-authored, in the manifest,
# seeded by athena-model into urn:chorus:instances under act — in the werk
# env at env-up and in prod at deploy-canonical. No hand runs.
#
# Jeff, 2026-09-02: "i expected all doc sections to be attributes in the class",
# then "we must do athena-* flow on these … using act … the pipeline". Spine
# carries its design-doc sections as the nine string properties #4045 added to
# ProductShape; the other eight fill theirs per card.
#
# Exported from the live store 2026-09-02 08:58 (dcterms provenance dropped —
# the seeder stamps its own), then spine's sections added. chorus:comment is
# emitted as both rdfs:comment (shape path) and chorus:comment (projection).
# =============================================================================

chorus:athena a chorus:Product ;
    chorus:comment """Athena is the structural and query layer of Chorus — the canonical model of what exists in the team's product world (products, domains, services, value-streams) and the predicates that connect them.""" ;
    rdfs:comment """Athena is the structural and query layer of Chorus — the canonical model of what exists in the team's product world (products, domains, services, value-streams) and the predicates that connect them.""" ;
    chorus:label """Athena""" ;
    rdfs:label """Athena""" ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-wren ;
    chorus:vision """A single SHACL-gated model whose one generator projects Product, Domain, Service, and ValueStream into uniform generated APIs and pages, made whole by construction through the DAL as the only write path.""" ;
    chorus:valueProposition """One queryable source of truth for the product tree with no fallback that yields a different answer, so every structural and impact question resolves to a real tree IRI rather than memory or pattern-matching.""" ;
    chorus:audience """Gates, SessionStart envelope injection, blast-radius, role-nudge routing, demo feedback, the tagging layer, and Jeff and the team via the rendered tree page.""" ;
    chorus:status """building""" ;
    chorus:gaps """A v1 predicate layer still being cleaned, the Service class not yet instantiated, and the generator not yet projecting inverse-path relationships as nested fields.""" ;
    chorus:atStep chorus:value-stream-step-designing ;
    chorus:hasDesignDoc chorus:document-athena-product-design ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:products, chorus:services, chorus:domains, chorus:value-streams ;
    chorus:promise """Athena is the structural and query layer of Chorus: the canonical model of what exists in the team's product world (products, domains, services, value-streams) and the predicates that connect them. It is what makes the chorus product tree queryable — every other product's structural placement (Loom's principles, Werk's pipelines, Borg's logs) is an Athena instance.
Athena is a product-and-design pipeline, not "a schema": the structural model (Product / Domain / Service) is the product layer; the narrative attributes (asIs / toBe / notInScope / hasDesignDoc and, since #4045, the nine design sections) are the design layer; the substrate is the pipeline — every instance under the same SHACL-gated contract, advancing through one artifact lifecycle (exploring → building → operating → retiring), rendered by the same UI.
Value: one source, multiple call shapes, no fallback path that produces a different answer. Consumers: the gates (/gate-product resolves a card's domain to a real tree IRI), SessionStart envelope injection, blast-radius, role-nudge routing (who owns this?), /demo feedback citing tree IRIs, Jeff and the team via the rendered pages, and the tagging layer (tree IRIs are the canonical tag enumeration for cards, code and tests).""" ;
    chorus:structure """Up: Athena is a Product of the Chorus product (partOf chorus; the recursive-Product model — a "subproduct" is just a Product that is the child of another Product). Down: Athena's substance is the union of its Domains; each Domain hosts its Services (where the code lives); the Product consumes the Services it depends on.
Domains served today: products, services, domains, value-streams — the four structural classes, each a domain whose page renders THE SET, the generated catalog live. (The 2026-05 design named domains / services / knowledge / domain-context; knowledge moved to pulse on 2026-09-02, #4045.)
Child products: none — Athena is a leaf Product.
Surfaces: the athena-* verbs (athena-model / athena-validate / athena-make / athena-deploy, MCP tools), the generated collection + entity APIs at :3360 (owl-api), the generated pages under /athena/ (products, domains, services, value-streams, class atlas), and the MCP tools chorus_tree_get / chorus_ownership_lookup / chorus_blast_radius.
Overlays (to-be): non-containment annotations — authority, ownership, deploy-route, customer-happiness — queryable as their own predicates. As-is Athena has no overlay surface.""" ;
    chorus:model """The structural model (Product / Domain / Service / ValueStream classes + their SHACL shapes) is value-stream-aligned — the domains support the stream — so it lives at the value-stream level: the generic shapes in value-stream-template.html (§5), Athena's instances in athena-value-stream-design.html (§3). Athena's product design references them and adds how the product serves its step and its surfaces. One model, many product surfaces over it; no inlining, no drift.
Source of record: roles/silas/ontology/chorus.ttl (the ontology) + the shapes it carries; the generator (owl-api) builds its serve list from definesVocabulary, so a served class is a claimed class by construction.
Invariants the model enforces at write time (the DAL, #3257): every required edge needs an existing target (Role, ValueStream, ValueStreamStep, seed Documents populate before any Product/Domain/Service can validate); a partial create is refused 422 — no half-written instances; retired predicates (inParent / inProduct / hostedBy / belongsTo / partOf back-pointers) return 409 naming the canonical replacement; edge removal refuses minCount violations. On #4045 ProductShape refused spine four times until gaps, atStep, hasDesignDoc and hasDomain were all real — the model enforced product-design-before-service-design without anyone remembering to.""" ;
    chorus:pagesAndFlow """Jeff's ruling (2026-06-12, #3378): "the pages and owl are all part of the athena product design." The UX is a flow of pages — landing (the value stream itself: steps + products) → step → product → domain → service — where every page is a rendering of its class's generated API plus its schema, and every inter-page link follows a real model edge. Navigation starts from the value stream, not products (the CMDB ruling, April).
Page anatomy (the review standard for every page until pages are generator-emitted): breadcrumb → identity → promise → stats → honest folds (a fold renders always; absent data says so) → provenance layer-labels → edges-are-links.
Live today under /athena/: products.html (tiles, with the design link), product.html?p=<name> (hero → vision → chapters; every property of the served Product schema, present or not, edges as links, hasDesignDoc resolved to the document's href — #4045), domains, services, value-streams, and the class atlas (#4053). Phone-first: tables stack on a phone (Jeff, 2026-09-02: "think about the ux of having a properties table on phone").""" ;
    chorus:apiSurface """Generated by owl-api at :3360, one resource namespace per structural class, served from urn:chorus:instances; every collection carries apiVersion / modelVersion / vocabVersion and the shape + commit it was generated from.
GET /products · /products/:name — Product list / instance with hasChild, hasDomain, consumes, atStep, hasDesignDoc edges; /products/openapi.json is the contract.
GET /domains · /domains/:name — Domain with its outbound edges and content instances by class; /domains/:name/has-child for the recursive containment.
GET /services · /services/:name — Service with dependencies, consumers, surfaces.
GET /value-streams · /value-stream-steps — the ValueStream / ValueStreamStep graph.
GET /documents — the served Document rows (hasDesignDoc targets).
Writes: POST/PUT on the same resources through the DAL (identity token required; SHACL the only gate) — PUT drops off-shape properties; there is no PATCH. Mutation attribution: every write emits a spine event with role + card + triple provenance.
Designed, not yet served (the 2026-05 v2 table): /athena/edges?subject=&predicate=&object= (predicate-pattern query), /athena/blast-radius/:id as a route (today computed inside the cards CLI), POST /athena/sparql read-only passthrough, overlay resources (/athena/overlay/*), and principle/practice invoke at a decision point.""" ;
    chorus:asIs """As stated in athena-product-design.html (restructured 2026-06-12) and refreshed by what the store serves on 2026-09-03 — not a full re-measurement:
Serving: the generated collection + entity APIs at :3360 for products (9), domains, services, value-streams, documents (18); the pages under /athena/; the athena-* verbs (athena-model / athena-validate / athena-make / athena-deploy) with the DAL as the write door; the MCP tools chorus_tree_get / chorus_ownership_lookup / chorus_blast_radius; SessionStart envelope injection; the tagging convention.
Instances travel through the pipeline: products, documents, roles, value-streams, pipelines are day-authored seed files in platform/config/instance-seed-manifest.txt, seeded by athena-model at env-up (werk store) and at land (prod) — no hand runs (#4045, #3838, #4040).
Known gaps carried from the design: the v1 predicate layer (hasDomain once double-declared, consumes overloaded, belongsTo used-but-undeclared) is being retired predicate by predicate; the Service layer is thin (chorus:Service barely instantiated); two vocabularies (chorus: / fw:) with no equivalence bridge; three naming schemes for graph identifiers (#1772); chorus:spine is one IRI typed Domain and Product (#1772); documents seed into urn:chorus:instances while /documents serves from urn:chorus:domains:documents (per-group graph pins, noted on #4062).""" ;
    chorus:toBe """One generator covers Product / Domain / Service / ValueStream uniformly — shapes are the generator's input; every class gets the same generated API + page treatment (largely landed for reads; pages are still hand-shelled over the generated API).
DAL writes as the only write path; SHACL the only gate; the graph whole by construction. A guard refuses the bash deployer from a role session outside act (#4062).
/ca <card> — the athena-* flow as one pipeline trigger, the /cw sibling for the model: model → validate → make → deploy-werk → demo → GO → deploy-canonical (#4062). A model-only card no longer needs a fake code change to be provable.
Doc corpus as graph citizens: every design doc a chorus:Document cited by IRI, and every product's design sections as Product attributes (spine #4045; the other eight #4080) — the HTML becomes a rendering, not the store.
Pages generated: the landing → step → product → domain → service flow emitted by the generator; the flow mock is the spec until then.
Overlays: authority / ownership / deploy-route / customer-happiness as first-class queryable annotation predicates.
Path: #3350 → #3373 → #3351 (done) → DAL #3257 (done) → #4045 (done) → #4080 → #4062 (/ca) → #1772 (one naming scheme) → overlays.""" ;
    chorus:notInScope """fw: vocabulary reconciliation — graph-wide, not Athena-specific; named as a gap, not solved here.
Gathering's data domains — CollectionDomain removed from Chorus; Photos / Music / Stories belong to Gathering's ontology, downstream (Convergence is the boundary).
The card pipeline — lives in the cards service (Clearing) with its own spine events; Athena's machinery is the artifact lifecycle only.
Observability of the running system — Borg's substrate.
Phase-2 placement (where v2 code, the renderer, and overlay graphs live) — its own card after data correctness closes.""" ;
    chorus:references """athena-product-design.html — Wren, 2026-05-15, restructured 2026-06-12 (#3378): identity / promise / structure / model / pages / API / as-is–to-be. The source of these sections.
athena-value-stream-design.html — Athena's value-stream instance (§3 the instances); value-stream-template.html — the generic shapes (§5).
ADR-040 — namespace + IRI-minting discipline (the DAL mints IRIs). ADR-028 — substrate-class domain contract. ADR-058 — model-only proving (option A).
reasoning-substrate-shift.html — Wren, 2026-05-14 — the master lever: make the graph as interrogable as the logs already are.
domain-model-asis-tobe.html — the predicate-layer + recursive-Domain refactor source. loom-subproduct-design.html — the first subproduct design; the structural layer was lifted from it. chorus-product-tree.html — product / step / domain intent set.
Cards: #3345 / #3350 (generated Domain API), #3351 (ValueStream), #3257 (DAL), #4045 (products in the pipeline; design sections as attributes), #4080 (this fill), #4062 (/ca), #1772 (one naming scheme).
Chorus · designing/docs/athena-product-design.html · #4080 · Wren · 2026-09-03""" ;
    chorus:publishesPreAuth """true""" ;
    chorus:partOf chorus:chorus .

chorus:borg a chorus:Product ;
    chorus:label """Borg""" ;
    rdfs:label """Borg""" ;
    chorus:comment """Borg is the self-judgment product of Chorus, spanning Proving and Reflecting — the system seeing itself so no human has to be the eyes.""" ;
    rdfs:comment """Borg is the self-judgment product of Chorus, spanning Proving and Reflecting — the system seeing itself so no human has to be the eyes.""" ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-silas ;
    chorus:vision """A model-driven reflect cycle where monitor and alert are ontology domains whose contracts generate, the page renders a verdict not a readout, and the capability travels generatively to run with chorus off.""" ;
    chorus:valueProposition """Borg's product isn't dashboards — it's Jeff's attention back: it surfaces the one thing that needs a person, calmly, to the owner, so no human is ever the first to notice a stall.""" ;
    chorus:audience """The roles (to self-coordinate and catch a dark peer, flapping service, or drift before Jeff does) and Jeff (outcomes only — a calm board, or the single thing that needs him).""" ;
    chorus:status """building""" ;
    chorus:gaps """Probes were bespoke and lied, there is no liveness or crash-loop signal, alerts are hand-routed, there is no model-driven contract, and there is no Borg page — the observation surfaces are scattered.""" ;
    chorus:atStep chorus:value-stream-step-proving ;
    chorus:hasDesignDoc chorus:document-borg-product-design ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:infrastructure, chorus:builds, chorus:deploys, chorus:time, chorus:heralds, chorus:toolchain, chorus:analytics, chorus:security, chorus:Properties, chorus:alerts-monitors, chorus:logs, chorus:identity, chorus:metrics ;
    chorus:promise """The system sees itself — so no human has to be the eyes. Borg reflects on everything it can reach (its services, health, alerts, the gap between how it is drawn and how it runs) and surfaces the one thing that needs a person, calmly, to the person who owns it.
Borg's product is not dashboards — it is your attention back. Every night Jeff is the first to notice a stall is a night Borg failed at its job. The freeze that hid for weeks (#3406) is the anti-promise made concrete.
Audience: the roles consume Borg to self-coordinate — notice a peer dark, a service flapping, a drift, before Jeff does; Borg is how the team becomes its own monitoring system. Jeff consumes outcomes only: a calm board, or the single thing that needs him. Never the 29-warning wall; never the role of monitor.""" ;
    chorus:structure """Borg spans two value-stream steps — same eye, two focal lengths: Proving (prove one change, per-card, terminates: present → gather → verdict → accept) and Reflecting (watch the running system, continuous, loops back to Shaping: plant → tend → read → surface → prune → feed). One self-judgment product at two cadences. In the store today Borg sits atStep Proving; the Reflecting span is a delta the design lands.
Domains (13 served today): alerts-monitors, analytics, builds, deploys, heralds, identity, infrastructure, logs, metrics, security, time, toolchain, and Properties. The design groups them in three layers — observability (heralds · monitor · alert · logs · metrics · analytics), operations (deploys · builds · time · security-trust), infrastructure (infra hosts · properties · toolchain) — and splits alerts-monitors into monitor + alert per ADR-043; that split and the grouping are to-be.
Owner: Silas, wearing all hats (PM / domain-architect / engineering-lead / operations-lead). Not greenfield: a running observability stack (Prometheus / Grafana / Loki / Alertmanager / exporters / deep-health) plus ADR-043; the design names the cycle over it.""" ;
    chorus:model """The monitor/alert domains, the six monitor types as Monitor subclasses, and the Service / Signal / Alert / SLO classes are defined in ADR-043 and seated in the value-stream spine (borg-value-stream-design.html §3). Source of record there, not re-asserted in the product design.
The coherence delta — declared model versus observed behaviour — is itself a first-class modeled thing; it is what most Borg pages render. The map (the /chorus system drawing: how the system is meant to cohere) versus the mirror (how it actually runs); the gap between them is the signal.
The verdict is computed, not curated: verdict = f(open alerts by severity, SLO burn-rate, liveness/freshness gaps) → calm when no critical alert is open, no SLO burns fast, and no monitored thing is silent past its freshness window; otherwise the one thing = the highest-severity unresolved signal.""" ;
    chorus:pagesAndFlow """Every Borg page is a generated page — the #3351 domain-page pattern, not a bespoke dashboard: a static shell projected by owl-api, the client fetching the generated HTTP routes, conforming to the #3415 design system. Explicitly generated, not hand-built — the scattered hand-built dashboards are exactly the problem.
Entry is through the system drawing, not a standalone dashboard: /chorus (the map) → the Spine node → Borg / Proving opens the mirror.
The landing is a verdict, not a readout. Two states: calm ("all coherent, nothing needs you — go") or the one thing that does, alone, with nothing competing for the eye. You walk into a room and know instantly if it is calm or on fire; the gauges are one drill down, not the front door. The antidote to the 29-warning wall.
The cycle renders as a seasonal wheel (plant → tend → read → surface → prune → feed), not a progress bar — that is Werk's line. Drill pages: Monitor (liveness, freshness, saturation, latency, error/crash-loop, synthetic flows — each renders the ADR-043 contract), Alert (firing / fired, severity, routed-to, dedup), Health / Metrics / Fitness (the aggregate verdict, SLO burn, the flow-report).
AX = JX: the agent (via the borg MCP tools) and the human (via the generated HTTP surface) read the same model.""" ;
    chorus:apiSurface """To-be routes generated by owl-api from the monitor / alert / SLO classes, named after the model:
GET /borg/verdict → {state: calm | one-thing, signal} — the landing; today improvised in the page.
GET /services/:name/monitors — typed monitor contract, model-driven; today deep-health.sh cron + /api/chorus/context/health.
GET /alerts?owner=&severity= — config / ownership-routed evaluator over the spine; today Alertmanager + alert-runner shell rules + /context/alerts.
GET /slo/:name/burn — SLI / SLO surfaces; today Prometheus :9090 + exporters.
GET /borg/flow — standing, page-rendered fitness; today chorus_flow_report (MCP). MCP and route share the model.
GET /services/:name/liveness — service.alive emit + absence detector (ADR-043 first build); today the gap that hid #3406.
Also live today under Chorus: the Loki log query surface (chorus_logs_query / logs_for_card / logs_for_trace), the pain rollup, and the nightly-suites red list the roles read each morning.""" ;
    chorus:asIs """As stated in borg-product-design.html (Silas, 2026-06-14) — not re-measured on 2026-09-03:
Deployed: a running stack (Prometheus / Grafana / Loki / Alertmanager / exporters / deep-health); ADR-043 landed (the domain model); #3405 landed (probe truthfulness — the cry-wolf killed); the 03:00 nightly is the red-main detector.
But: probes were bespoke and lied; no liveness / crash-loop signal (why #3406 hid); alerts hand-routed; no model-driven contract; no Borg page — the observation surfaces are scattered.
Since the design (from the spine and the 2026-08/09 journals): membrane test bootouts killed the nightlies for weeks before being named (#3720); the products graph was wiped by a nightly run from a werk (2026-08-28) and restored from MODEL_SET; role state is now derived from the streams rather than declared (#4028); the pain rollup re-reports fixed classes unless read per day.""" ;
    chorus:toBe """The borg-reflect cycle, model-driven: monitor / alert as ontology domains whose contracts generate; the verdict-first Borg page; absence and silence first-class signals.
Path to close (ordered): value-stream spine → liveness leg (the #3406 gap) → freshness / errors / saturation / latency / synthetic legs → config-driven alert routing → the Borg pages render it.
Mitosis, the commercial bet: Borg is built to travel. Chorus is a factory; the systems it builds must run with chorus OFF — so Borg's capability ships generatively (the model generates the client system's scrape configs, alert rules, SLO defs, dashboards, liveness emitters, deploy/rollback scripts) plus a standalone OSS stack. The gate is a literal test: turn chorus off — does the client system still observe / alert / deploy itself? Any callback to chorus is a leaked dependency to cut. Borg is the exemplar of "model anything → build anything"; gathering is client #0.
Parked: the observability corpus as an ML / training substrate, once the telemetry is modeled, flowing and trustworthy.""" ;
    chorus:notInScope """The demo ceremony tooling (werk-demo orchestration, present → gather → verdict → accept) — Werk's. The per-card proving judgment IS in scope: Borg proves; Werk runs the ceremony.
Remediation / acting in the Reflecting half — Borg surfaces, the owning role prunes (observe-only). Borg's operations layer does act (deploy / rollback / restart); reflect-not-act is an observability property, not the whole product's.
Assimilate / mitose — the other two Borg modes (ICD legacy extraction, reproducing across products) are modeled in their own docs; they share this product's herald / xray as their first step.
/flow — Directing, not Proving.""" ;
    chorus:references """borg-product-design.html — Silas, 2026-06-14, DRAFT: the spine of these sections (identity / promise / structure / model / pages / API / as-is–to-be / not-in-scope / mitosis).
borg-value-stream-design.html — the reflect cycle + the domains; drives the product design. athena-product-design.html — the mirror-this instance.
ADR-043 — monitor / alert split, the six monitor types, Service / Signal / Alert / SLO. observability-service-design.html, logs-service-design.html, infrastructure-service-design.html.
chorus-product-domain-hierarchy.html — the full domain model. GOOD_BORG.html, BORG_ASSIMILATION_PATTERN.html, borg-mitosis.html — the three modes.
Cards: #3418 (cycle / garden / MAPE-K + permaculture / map↔mirror / verdict-not-readout), #3415 (design system), #3406 (the freeze that hid), #3405 (probe truthfulness), #3720 (nightly black box), #4028 (role state derived from streams).
Chorus · designing/docs/borg-product-design.html · #4080 · Wren (fill) / Silas (design) · 2026-09-03""" ;
    chorus:publishesPreAuth """true""" ;
    chorus:partOf chorus:chorus .

chorus:chorus a chorus:Product ;
    chorus:label """Chorus""" ;
    rdfs:label """Chorus""" ;
    chorus:comment """The coordination protocol — hooks, scripts, gates, dashboards, spine, shared memory index. The nervous system.""" ;
    rdfs:comment """The coordination protocol — hooks, scripts, gates, dashboards, spine, shared memory index. The nervous system.""" ;
    chorus:ownedBy """role-wren""" ;
    chorus:vision """A multi-agent/human team that builds a platform for building systems — coordination itself modeled, observable, improvable.""" ;
    chorus:valueProposition """Three AI roles and one human work as a real team: shared memory, one board, one audit spine, gates at the right moments.""" ;
    chorus:audience """Jeff and the three roles, and future teams adopting the method.""" ;
    chorus:status """operating""" ;
    chorus:gaps """hasDesignDoc unfilled (no Document instances in graph). V1/V2 domain-layer convergence outstanding.""" ;
    chorus:atStep chorus:value-stream-step-directing ;
    chorus:hasDesignDoc chorus:document-chorus-as-platform ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:search, chorus:memory ;
    chorus:promise """Chorus is a platform in the oldest sense of the word: its product is not a feature, it is a method of building. A system that builds systems — and the people building inside it happen to be AI agents, working alongside one human. Everything it produces is downstream of a single bet: get the way you build right, and what you build follows.
The proof that this is more than a slogan: the system generates large parts of itself. The same model that describes Chorus is the model it uses to generate its own interfaces, tests and the scaffolding of its own actions, from one source. What is generated is the shape, the contract, the wiring; the logic inside those actions is still written by hand.
What you would adopt: not an app but the method — a repeatable, instrumented, legible way to forge software, with a small team of human and agents working the cycle. For the team itself: shared memory — any role can ask "what happened last session?" or "what does the team know about photos?" and get a semantically rich answer without asking Jeff.""" ;
    chorus:structure """Chorus is THE top-level value stream, recursive: Shaping → Directing → Designing → Building → Proving → Reflecting. Each step encapsulates a product's value stream: Loom (Shaping), Clearing + Spine + Pulse (Directing), Athena (Designing), Werk (Building), Borg (Proving + Reflecting), Convergence (the boundary). The products are peers of one another and children of the Chorus product (partOf chorus).
The grammar underneath is small: nouns (a domain, a product, a piece of work — things with structure and identity), verbs (commit, deploy, register, run — a small fixed set), events (what a verb gives off when it fires — how the system sees itself). Nouns and verbs are peers; you compose on need, never in advance. Each element performs many functions; each function is supported by many elements.
Domains served on the chorus product today: memory, search — the shared-memory substrate (the SQLite FTS index, the LanceDB vector index, the HTTP API on :3340, the hooks service, the ingestion pipelines). The other domains live on the child products.
Team: three persistent AI roles (Wren — PM / interaction layer; Silas — architect / observation layer; Kade — engineer / presentation layer) plus Jeff as owner. A role is defined by what it is accountable for: the nouns it owns and the verbs it performs. Each role runs its own streams and helps build the shared platform.""" ;
    chorus:model """The Chorus model is the value-stream model: ValueStream → ValueStreamStep → Product → Domain → Service, with Product and Domain recursive via hasChild, one containment predicate per meaning (hasDomain: Product → Domain; consumes: Product → Service; atStep: Product → ValueStreamStep; ownedBy → Role), every class with a SHACL shape, the DAL the only write path. Source of record: roles/silas/ontology/chorus.ttl + shapes; served by owl-api from urn:chorus:instances.
One standard, many owners: each domain's owner defines that domain's own data — the person closest to it knows it best. What is held in common is the standard every definition must meet (the shapes, the IRI discipline of ADR-040, the emit contract of ADR-046), not the definitions themselves. The anti-pattern avoided on purpose: one architect designing everyone's data.
A domain is an owl:Class (ADR-045); a verb has a contract (ADR-032); the repo is recursive (ADR-041). Roles, value streams, products, documents, pipelines are seed files in the instance manifest, deployed through the pipeline — the model is reproducible, not live-only.""" ;
    chorus:pagesAndFlow """The method is a cycle, not a pipeline, and the pages follow it. /chorus is the system drawing (the map); from it the value stream (/athena/value-streams), then the products (/athena/products.html — nine tiles, each with its design link), then each product's page (/athena/product.html?p=<name>: hero → vision → chapters), then its domains and services. Every page renders its class's generated API; every link follows a real model edge.
The Clearing (:3470) is the surface Jeff actually looks at: role tiles, the message stream, session tails, alerts, multi-party chat — from any device, including his phone over the tunnel.
The Loom pages (/loom/principles, /loom/policies) render the normative layer — every rule credits its principle (#4077).
Search: /chorus search over team memory (sessions, spine, briefs, decisions, Clearing messages) — the search hierarchy DEC-074: Chorus first, then the graph, then the filesystem.""" ;
    chorus:apiSurface """The Chorus API on :3340 — the single front door for programmatic access (DEC-093; never :3000, that is the app):
GET /api/chorus/search?q=&channel=&order=&limit= — hybrid FTS + vector search over 13 source types; GET /api/chorus/health; GET /api/chorus/conversations; GET /api/chorus/freshness (per-source, 30s cache).
GET /api/chorus/context/{board/wip, roles, health, alerts, spine} — the per-prompt context endpoints; GET /api/chorus/knowledge/{domains, domains/:name, search}.
GET /api/loom/principles, /api/loom/policies — the normative layer. GET /api/athena/* — the legacy athena reads (health, subdomains, blast-radius, owners, machines).
The generated model APIs at :3360 (owl-api): /products, /domains, /services, /value-streams, /documents, /tests — see Athena.
MCP: one typed tool per verb (werk-pull … werk-accept, chorus_werk, athena-model / -validate / -make / -deploy, chorus_cards_*, chorus_nudge_message, chorus_logs_*, chorus_principles_*). The surface is pinned by a contract test — adding a verb is a conscious pin edit (#3329).
Hooks: chorus-hooks (Rust) on a unix socket intercepts every tool call — PreToolUse gates, per-prompt context injection, Stop-hook policies (word cap, nudge trap), telemetry to the spine.""" ;
    chorus:asIs """As stated in chorus-service-design.html (2026-04-11, updated 2026-04-18) and chorus-as-platform.html (2026-08), plus what runs on 2026-09-03 — not a full re-measurement:
Running: the Chorus API on :3340; the FTS index (~/.chorus/index.db) fed continuously by the session indexer and bridge subscribers; the vector index (LanceDB + Ollama nomic-embed-text on Bedroom); chorus-hooks injecting Pulse / Spine / Athena context into every prompt; the spine (~/.chorus/chorus.log, append-only, never rotated — Jeff's ruling 2026-07-23); the Clearing; the board (Vikunja + the cards CLI); the werk pipeline (act + werk.yml); owl-api serving the generated model; the nightly suites at 03:00 and 06:00.
The honest frontier (chorus-as-platform §8): self-regulation. All four lenses (permaculture, Team Topologies, cybernetics, rhizome) describe a system that holds its own health; Chorus has the structure of that system but not yet the reflex. Today, when something drifts, a human still tends to notice first.
Known gaps from the service design still open in shape: eight data sources without ingestion pipelines (code, tests, git history, logs, state files, alert rules, skills, Vikunja); staleness alerting binary; no reindex endpoint. Delivery of a message into a session (clearing-surface) remains the cross-cutting flaky part.""" ;
    chorus:toBe """Close the reflex gap: the system senses and corrects its own operational health before a person has to (Borg's verdict + liveness legs; role state derived from streams, #4028; Pulse derived not declared).
Everything through the pipeline: code via /cw (chorus_werk), the model via /ca (#4062), the daily rhythm via the scheduler — one uniform verb interface, the conductor rented (act, launchd), never an orchestration engine of our own (chorus-as-platform §4).
Every design doc a graph citizen: the nine products carry their design sections as attributes (spine #4045, the eight #4080); pages become renderings of the model.
Team memory complete: the missing ingestion pipelines (code, tests, commits, logs, state files, skills, board) so "where is the photo handler?" and "what changed yesterday?" are semantic queries; per-source freshness with graduated severity; a reindex endpoint.
The commercial shape (chorus-as-platform §9, Borg §10): a client takes the method, not an app — the factory generates the commodity substrate (~80%: structure + the ilities); human craft goes to the differentiated behaviour. Gathering is client #0.""" ;
    chorus:notInScope """Gathering's application features (photos, garden, music, people) — Gathering is the product Chorus builds and client #0 of the factory; its data domains belong to its own ontology.
The individual products' internals — each of Athena, Borg, Clearing, Convergence, Loom, Pulse, Spine, Werk carries its own design sections; this row is the platform frame only.
Hosted per-PR CI — cost-killed 2026-04-29 (#2600); the merge gate is local act + Jeff's GO (ADR-053), the nightly is the red-main detector.
A bespoke orchestration engine — rent the conductor (act, launchd, a data-flow engine for ingestion); build only the connective tissue.""" ;
    chorus:references """chorus-as-platform.html — Wren, 2026-08: "A System to Build Systems" — the product is the method; the grammar (nouns / verbs / events); the cycle; rent the conductor; one standard many owners; how the team is composed; the four influences; the honest frontier. The source of the promise, structure and to-be here.
chorus-service-design.html — Silas 2026-04-11 / Wren 2026-04-18 (#1877, #2168): the shared-memory substrate — FTS, vector index, HTTP API, hooks service, ingestion pipelines, the data-source inventory. The source of the API surface and as-is here.
chorus-reference-model.html, why-and-how-of-chorus.html, system-model-thinking.html, cybernetic-systems-chorus.html, chorus-nervous-system.html, HOMEOSTASIS_RESEARCH.html — what Chorus is.
value-stream-design.html, value-stream-template.html, chorus-value-stream-deep-dive.html — how it builds. chorus-spine.html — the value-stream sense of spine.
self-model-owl-framework.html, owl-spec-as-source-flow.html, chorus-product-domain-hierarchy.html, chorus-domain-decomposition.html — the model.
chorus-wardley.html, chorus-consulting.html, chorus-distribution-assessment.html — strategy. ADR-032 (verb contract), ADR-041 (recursive repo), ADR-045 (a domain is an owl:Class), ADR-046 (emit contract), ADR-053 (merge gate), DEC-074 (search hierarchy), DEC-093 (domain endpoints).
Chorus · designing/docs/chorus-as-platform.html · #4080 · Wren · 2026-09-03""" ;
    chorus:publishesPreAuth """true""" .

chorus:clearing a chorus:Product ;
    chorus:label """The Clearing""" ;
    rdfs:label """The Clearing""" ;
    chorus:comment """Multi-party real-time alignment — browser chat with Jeff and all three AI roles. Parent product of Spine and Pulse.""" ;
    rdfs:comment """Multi-party real-time alignment — browser chat with Jeff and all three AI roles. Parent product of Spine and Pulse.""" ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-wren ;
    chorus:vision """One shared room where the team aligns in minutes instead of relaying briefs, with every DECISION: line landing in the graph automatically.""" ;
    chorus:valueProposition """Real-time multi-party alignment with decisions captured where they happen — Jeff stops being the transport layer between role terminals.""" ;
    chorus:audience """Jeff and all three roles during alignment moments. Borg reads the transcripts, and decisions marked in-channel are captured to the decision log.""" ;
    chorus:status """operating""" ;
    chorus:gaps """hasDesignDoc unfilled (no Document instances in graph). Transcript indexing depends on the index-freshness pipeline that alerts today.""" ;
    chorus:atStep chorus:value-stream-step-directing ;
    chorus:hasDesignDoc chorus:document-clearing-value-stream-design ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:cards, chorus:streams, chorus:messages ;
    chorus:promise """The Clearing is the team's I/O layer: how the team and the running system talk and track work. Three faces — the board (input: what we choose to do), the comms (output: how it reaches a session), and the spine (record: what happened). It is the seat where the team and the machine meet: Jeff's board choices and the products' emits land in the same log.
Jeff's experience (clearing-service-design, 2026-04-06): "The place where I see the team working in real time. Role tiles show who's building what, the message stream shows decisions and demos as they happen, and alerts surface without me checking terminals. When the Clearing works, I manage by glancing. When it breaks, I'm back to checking three terminals and guessing who's stuck."
Clearing is a SUBSTRATE, not a line or a loop — every other product borrows it for its messages (nudge / surface / inject are Clearing's verbs) and every verb's trace/emit lands in Clearing's spine.""" ;
    chorus:structure """The Directing-step instance. Product Clearing composes the domains cards, messages, streams (served today); the value-stream design names six across the three faces — board (cards, chunks, tags, states, WIP limits: Vikunja + the cards CLI), messages (nudges, the bridge/stream, peer chat: the messaging API :3475), delivery (the inject substrate: chorus-inject), context (per-prompt context synthesis: the context-inject hook), spine (the append-only event log) and events (the event grammar: spine-events.json). Spine has since become its own Product (#4045) with the events domain; Pulse is Clearing's child product (the short-term memory layer).
Verb family (clearing-*): board — card, chunk, tag, prioritize (rank chunks by value, WSJF), sequence (order cards by dependency, a topological sort — deliberately separate from prioritize), sweep, wip; comms — nudge (persist AND deliver, DEC-107), surface (push a message into a session / to Jeff — the load-bearing delivery verb), inject, gather; spine — tail.
Ownership: Wren the model and the coordination (board taxonomy, verb model, comms contracts, the event grammar); Kade the presentation (the board render, the WIP tile, the group-chat surface); Silas the spine substrate (emit SDK, log infra, conformance gate).""" ;
    chorus:model """Clearing's heart is a Kanban flow system whose system of record is an event-sourced log. Cards are pulled through workflow states (Next → WIP → Done) under WIP limits; every board op and every comms op appends an immutable event to the spine; the board you see is a projection built by folding those events. The board is a read-model; the spine is the truth (Young's CQRS, Kreps' The Log).
Content classes: Card (with its cross-axis tags — domain / type / origin / sequence / chunk — and its AC + Experience, validated at pull), Message / Nudge (persist + deliver, the From/To envelope), Stream, Session (the session registry: ~/.chorus/sessions/<role>-<pid>.json routes delivery), Role state (now DERIVED from agent.activity + the streams, #4028 — the declared file is gone).
The first Service instance in the graph was chorus:service-clearing (#3675); the service-design page derives from it (GET :3360/services) and must not contradict it. Governing decisions: DEC-107 (both delivery paths every time — locked, do not reopen), DEC-048 (proving gate: deploy, demo to Jeff, accept), DEC-093 (domain endpoints on :3340), DEC-1571 (attention contract: announce + continue).""" ;
    chorus:pagesAndFlow """The Clearing (:3470, Express + Socket.IO, LaunchAgent com.chorus.clearing; public door via Cloudflare tunnel): six components — Role Tiles (Jeff, Wren, Silas, Kade: state + card + last action, pushed via Socket.IO), Message Stream (classified, whitelist-only visibility — Jeff input, demos, blocks, decisions visible; protocol noise hidden), Session Tailer (live tail of each role's terminal, collapsible), Alerts Panel (severity-filterable, additive to the terminal nudge), Multi-Party Chat (/clearing; DECISION: prefix auto-captured; image + voice upload), Remote Access (token auth on the tunnel, guest names, local/LAN no auth).
Every demo variant now runs its own Clearing on 3481/3482/3483 pointed at the variant API, writing only werk-local files (#4075) — a test can no longer post into Jeff's room.
The board: Vikunja at :3456 for the human view; all mutations through the cards CLI, never the Vikunja API. Pulse tiles and /api/chorus/context/roles read the derived state.
Flow: Jeff files a card (/card, Jeff-initiated, no bouncer) or a role proposes one (bouncer → approval-ask) → /pull moves it to WIP and mints the werk → the pipeline emits card.pulled / card.demoed / card.accepted into the spine → the tiles and the stream render the projection → nudges deliver the handoffs.""" ;
    chorus:apiSurface """Board: the cards CLI (platform/scripts/cards: list, view, add, move, done, set, tag) and the MCP tools chorus_cards_add / _move / _done / _set / _tag / _view, chorus_card_add_jeff, chorus_wip, chorus_flow_report; GET /api/chorus/context/board/wip?role=.
Messages: the messaging API on :3475 (persist; history + team-scan drain) and chorus_nudge_message (persist AND deliver — osascript / tty / tmux transports via the session registry, ADR-039); GET /api/chorus/context/roles.
Clearing server (:3470): POST /api/message (bridge; alerts and role messages), POST /api/sessions, Socket.IO for tiles / stream / chat, GET / health; local-only admin and metrics; the OG image open for link previews.
Spine: chorus-log <event> <role> k=v… (the emit), chorus_logs_query / _for_card / _for_trace / _recent_errors (the read); GET /api/chorus/context/spine?limit=.
Context: the UserPromptSubmit hook drains the messaging queue + pulse + spine + Athena into every role's turn (chorus-context envelope).""" ;
    chorus:asIs """As stated in clearing-service-design.html (refreshed 2026-07-23, #3676) and clearing-value-stream-design.html (2026-06-21), plus the 2026-09-02 landings — not re-measured on 2026-09-03:
Live and proven end-to-end 2026-07-23: phone → clearing.lightlifeurbangardens.com → a locked-screen wren session over the tmux pane-first transport (#3668). Outbound delivery rides pulse through the session registry (tty / vscode / tmux). The WebSocket bridge token is enforced on tunneled traffic (#3669 lane 1). Clearing closed to unauthenticated network callers (#3966).
The board runs on Vikunja + the cards CLI; the spine is the append-only log; the comms are the MCP nudge path + chorus-inject; per-variant Clearings for demos (#4075); role state derived from the streams (#4028).
Open gaps: no per-participant authentication on the public door (#3669 lanes 2–3, Solid-OIDC via #3613); share.* export unreliable; delivery to agents is terminal injection rather than subscription (Buzz spike #3674: adopt / steal-the-pattern / pass); the verb family (clearing-*) is named in the design but not modeled — the mechanisms exist, the model does not; 20 Clearing browser specs skip until CLEARING_URL points at the variant room; /api/loom-metrics reads a 4 MB spine tail dominated by inject-response lines.""" ;
    chorus:toBe """Author the value-stream spine: value-stream-clearing + the three faces' verbs as ValueStreamSteps, in the model (the naming/modeling layer over mechanisms that exist).
Model the event grammar: re-seat spine-events.json as the events domain so emitters and registry rows generate together (now Spine's #4046).
Harden clearing-surface: delivery reliability is the whole-team payoff because every product borrows it — receipts (nudge.received / nudge.acted, #2708), retry on silence (#3363), the From/To envelope (#3112).
Build clearing-wip: enrich the WIP readout with the live pipeline strip from the spine emits — the first tile projecting a trace.
Generate the board view: the board render becomes a projection of the model + spine (the athena-make path applied to Clearing's surfaces; #2159 the Chorus-native board hierarchy).
Per-participant identity on the public door (#3669); a real-browser prod canary for Jeff's loop (#3871).""" ;
    chorus:notInScope """Card content and priority calls — Jeff's and the PM's; Clearing carries the board, it does not decide it.
The spine's own product (types, instances, reach) — Spine (#4045 / #4046 / #4044). Aggregation, dashboards, alert rules — Borg.
Pulse's composition (the hot register over cards / messages / alerts / events) — Pulse, Clearing's child product.
Identity (who a principal is) — the identity seam (#3613); Clearing consumes it.""" ;
    chorus:references """clearing-value-stream-design.html — Wren, 2026-06-21 (#3545): the three faces, the clearing-* verb family, the event-sourced engine, the six domains, ownership, sequencing, the operating-model frames (Kanban, WSJF, topological sort, Event Sourcing). The source of promise / structure / model / to-be here.
clearing-service-design.html — Wren, 2026-04-06 (#2287), refreshed 2026-07-23 (#3676): the six components, supporting domains, infrastructure, consumers, tests. The source of pages / API / as-is here.
value-stream-template.html — the generic pattern. streams-service-design.html, cards-service-design.html, nudge-service-design.html, service-design-pulse.html — the domain service designs.
DEC-107 (persist + deliver), DEC-048, DEC-093, DEC-1571 (attention contract), ADR-039 (transports). Cards: #3544 / #3548 (surface hardening), #3668 (tmux transport), #3669 (auth lanes), #3674 (Buzz spike), #4075 (per-variant Clearing), #4028 (derived role state), #3966 (Clearing closed to the network), #2159 (Chorus-native board).
Chorus · designing/docs/clearing-value-stream-design.html · #4080 · Wren · 2026-09-03""" ;
    chorus:publishesPreAuth """true""" ;
    chorus:partOf chorus:chorus .

chorus:convergence a chorus:Product ;
    chorus:label """Convergence""" ;
    rdfs:label """Convergence""" ;
    chorus:comment """Cross-domain integration — ICDs, harvesters, data pipelines. The product whose job is making the many sources one graph.""" ;
    rdfs:comment """Cross-domain integration — ICDs, harvesters, data pipelines. The product whose job is making the many sources one graph.""" ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-kade ;
    chorus:vision """Every outside source lands through one governed ingestion path — mapped, reconciled, and conformed to the canonical model before it enters the graph, so nothing arrives unshaped.""" ;
    chorus:valueProposition """Harvesters and pipelines governed by ICDs — every integration is declared before it is coded, so data lineage is a contract rather than an accident.""" ;
    chorus:audience """The roles as integration authors, the graph as the destination, the ICD gate as the enforcement point.""" ;
    chorus:status """building""" ;
    chorus:gaps """hasDesignDoc unfilled (no Document instances in graph). V1/V2 domain IRI duplication outstanding. Change-management engine (impact, propagate, verify) not yet built.""" ;
    chorus:atStep chorus:value-stream-step-building ;
    chorus:hasDesignDoc chorus:document-convergence-value-stream-design ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:integrations ;
    chorus:promise """Convergence is the boundary: it takes data from heterogeneous outside sources (an existing system, a legacy schema, an external feed) and brings it into the model, reconciled and conformed. Where Athena projects the model outward (generate), Convergence pulls the world inward (integrate). They share the same membrane — the OWL model / canonical form — approached from opposite sides.
Three verbs: ingest → map → land, event-triggered by incoming data, produces-and-terminates per batch. The load-bearing verb is land, and its heart is the RECONCILE, not the write. Jeff's thirty-year integration lesson: "always reconcile before loading — source data never matches cleanly." A land that skips reconciliation loads dirty, duplicated, unconformed data and corrupts the model it was supposed to enrich.
It is also the natural home of Borg's assimilation mode: the herald / xray discovers an existing system's structure, and Convergence is how that discovered data lands in the graph.""" ;
    chorus:structure """A LINE, the inbound twin of Athena. Owner: Kade (the ingestion — harvesters, the ingest / map / reconcile pipeline, source registrations, the extraction moves); Silas the OWL / SHACL floor the reconciled data must conform to (the canonical model + the ICD gate); Wren the model shapes / the value-stream design.
Domain served today: integrations. The value-stream design names five that follow the pipeline — sources (registered inbound systems + native schemas: to-be), icd (Interface Control Documents, the provider/consumer contracts per domain: partial — the gate runs), harvesters (the ingest workers, the harvest-* scripts and the gathering harvesters: live), mappings (source-schema → canonical transforms: to-be), reconciliation (cleanse / dedup / entity-resolution rules + the golden master + source→row mapping: to-be).
The step it recurses under is open (a Harvesting / boundary step, or cross-stream). Orchestrated by a chorus_convergence loop (the chorus_werk / chorus_athena analog), one trigger per inbound batch — to-be.""" ;
    chorus:model """A flow of tracked data units through a transform graph into a reconciled system of record. Data arrives as explicit packets carrying provenance (Flow-Based Programming; NiFi FlowFiles); it is routed and mapped toward one canonical form (Enterprise Integration Patterns: Message Translator, Content-Based Router, Normalizer, Canonical Data Model); before it lands it is reconciled against what is already there (record linkage: schema-map, cleanse, dedup, entity-resolve to a golden master plus a mapping of which sources fed which row).
ETL vs ELT is a map decision: transform-before-land (governance-first; our likely default given the OWL / SHACL floor) vs land-raw-then-transform. Canonical-model conformance is non-negotiable; where it runs is the choice.
Provenance is first-class: every unit retraces to its source — essential for a system that assimilates existing systems and must explain where each fact came from.
The ICD gate (DEC-095) is the write-door floor: no harvester code without a matching ICD provider section (icd-gate-hook.sh blocks writes to *-harvester.service.ts and harvest-*.sh without one; populate icd-instance-{domain}.ttl first). Mapper before harvest: no data loading without validated ICDs and semantic mapping.""" ;
    chorus:pagesAndFlow """Designed, not built: Convergence is the least-drafted of the six streams and has no page of its own today. The read surfaces that exist are Athena's — the integrations domain page under /athena/domains, the ICD comparison and process-flow notes (ICD_COMPARE_NOTES.html, ICD_PROCESS_FLOW.html, ICD_TEST_STRATEGY.html), the Wardley map of the ICD (WARDLEY_MAP_ICD.html), and the crawler dependency map (crawler-dependency-map.html).
The to-be flow, from the value-stream design: a source is registered (sources) → its ICD provider section is authored and validated (icd) → the harvester ingests tracked units with provenance (harvesters) → map routes and translates toward the canonical model (mappings) → reconcile conforms, cleanses, dedups and resolves entities (reconciliation) → land writes conformant instances into the graph, each fact retraceable to its origin. Each stage a generated domain page over its class, per the #3351 pattern.""" ;
    chorus:apiSurface """Today: the generated integrations domain reads at :3360 (/domains/integrations); the ICD instance graph urn:gathering:icd/current read via Fuseki; the gathering harvesters (harvest-*.sh, *-harvester.service.ts) as the ingest workers; NiFi on Bedroom for the photo pipeline (down as of the 2026-06 inventory — #3368 revives it).
To-be (the value-stream design): a chorus_convergence trigger (MCP) mirroring chorus_werk / chorus_athena — ingest → map → land per batch, with typed refusals at the reconcile gate; generated routes for /sources, /icd, /harvesters, /mappings, /reconciliation over their classes; a provenance query (which sources fed this row) as a read surface.
Guarded today: the ICD gate hook (DEC-095) on harvester writes; the membrane (#3615) refusing prod-surface writes from test/build contexts.""" ;
    chorus:asIs """As stated in convergence-value-stream-design.html (Wren, 2026-06-21, DRAFT 0.1) — not re-measured on 2026-09-03:
Convergence exists mostly as cards and intent (#3392 ICD / convergence TTLs → chorus tree + Fuseki load-path; #2291 Chorus extraction from Gathering), not a built pipeline. The ICD gate + the gathering harvesters are the closest running pieces. The photo harvest pipeline (NiFi on Bedroom) is to be revived (#3368).
Status in the store: building; one domain (integrations); owner Kade.
What the design got from Jeff: reconcile-before-load as the non-negotiable; Convergence as the inbound twin of Athena; the factory rule — what Convergence ingests must not shackle the products Chorus builds (the "turn Chorus off, does gathering still boot?" test).""" ;
    chorus:toBe """Author the value-stream spine: value-stream-convergence + ingest / map / land as ValueStreamSteps. Land it (greenfield).
ICD-first (DEC-095): the contract precedes the code; icd is the write-door floor.
One source end-to-end: pick one inbound domain (e.g. the #3392 ICD / convergence TTLs), run ingest → map → reconcile → land fully, proving the reconcile gate. The repetition is the rest of Convergence.
Golden master + provenance: entity resolution to one canonical record + a source→row mapping, so every landed fact retraces to its origin.
Generate the mappings where possible: the source→canonical transform is itself a model artifact (the athena-make path applied to integration), so mappings do not drift from the schema.
Convergence brings outside data into the model at author/build time; it must not become a runtime dependency of the products.""" ;
    chorus:notInScope """The canonical model itself (OWL / SHACL) — Silas's floor and Athena's product; Convergence lands into it.
Gathering's application logic over the ingested data — Gathering's.
Discovery of an existing system's structure (the herald / xray) — Borg's assimilation mode; Convergence lands what it finds.
A runtime coupling between Gathering and Chorus — explicitly refused: the relationship is generative (ingest-and-conform).""" ;
    chorus:references """convergence-value-stream-design.html — Wren, 2026-06-21 (#3545), DRAFT 0.1: the ingest → map → land cycle, the engine, the five domains, ownership, sequencing, the operating-model frames. The source of every section here.
CONVERGENCE_ARCHITECTURE.html — the earlier convergence architecture (DEC-096: a Chorus product artifact). value-stream-template.html — the generic pattern; athena-value-stream-design.html — the outbound twin.
ICD_PROCESS_FLOW.html, ICD_COMPARE_NOTES.html, ICD_TEST_STRATEGY.html, WARDLEY_MAP_ICD.html — the ICD substrate. crawler-dependency-map.html, crawler-service-design.html — the crawler lane. BORG_ASSIMILATION_PATTERN.html — assimilation.
Flow-Based Programming (J. Paul Morrison); Apache NiFi; Enterprise Integration Patterns (Hohpe & Woolf); ETL vs ELT; record linkage / entity resolution.
DEC-095 (ICD gate; mapper before harvest). Cards: #3392, #2291, #3368 (revive NiFi), #3615 (membrane).
Chorus · designing/docs/convergence-value-stream-design.html · #4080 · Wren · 2026-09-03""" ;
    chorus:publishesPreAuth """true""" ;
    chorus:partOf chorus:chorus .

chorus:loom a chorus:Product ;
    chorus:label """Loom""" ;
    rdfs:label """Loom""" ;
    chorus:comment """The operating-model and team-knowledge layer of Chorus — the team's persistent product memory at the Shaping step — carrying principles, practices, policies, decisions, roles, skills, and RCAs.""" ;
    rdfs:comment """The operating-model and team-knowledge layer of Chorus — the team's persistent product memory at the Shaping step — carrying principles, practices, policies, decisions, roles, skills, and RCAs.""" ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-jeff ;
    chorus:vision """A coherent product modeled on the recursive Athena model, one clean predicate set, every content type a real OWL class with a SHACL shape, every subdomain populated or explicitly planned — Loom as the template the other products follow.""" ;
    chorus:valueProposition """Loom gives the team one coherent, validated home for its normative substrate as real OWL classes with SHACL shapes, so the operating model is graphed and constrained rather than scattered as ungraphed markdown.""" ;
    chorus:audience """The Chorus team — the three AI roles and Jeff — for whom Loom holds the persistent operating frame; secondarily any future team adopting Chorus, who receives a working normative model rather than a pile of docs.""" ;
    chorus:status """exploring""" ;
    chorus:gaps """5 of 7 intent subdomains are empty shells (decisions live as ungraphed markdown; Decision and RCA aren't OWL classes); the predicate layer needs cleaning; content is unconstrained by SHACL.""" ;
    chorus:atStep chorus:value-stream-step-shaping ;
    chorus:hasDesignDoc chorus:document-loom-subproduct-design ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:rcas, chorus:roles, chorus:principles, chorus:policies, chorus:practices, chorus:skills, chorus:decisions ;
    chorus:promise """Loom is the operating-model / team-knowledge layer of Chorus — "the team's persistent product memory." Its domains carry the normative substrate: principles, practices, policies, decisions, roles, skills, RCAs. Three AI roles and one human coordinate without Jeff becoming the relay: briefs route directly, cards flow through gates, skills encode repeatable actions, decisions persist as governance. When this breaks, Jeff becomes a switchboard operator.
Loom is a LOOP at the Shaping step: the principles are the source, the practices express them, the policies enforce them with gates and hooks, and what the running system teaches (RCAs, retros, Jeff's corrections) feeds back into the principles. Every policy credits its principle (#4077); the principles are injected live into every role's boot envelope — do not paraphrase or cache locally, drift starts the moment you do.""" ;
    chorus:structure """Up: Loom is a Product of the Chorus product (partOf chorus), at the Shaping step, status exploring, owned by Jeff in the 2026-05 design and served ownedBy Wren today. Down: seven domains served — principles, practices, policies, decisions, roles, skills, rcas — exactly Jeff's intent set (2026-05-14), which the 2026-05 audit found the graph had grown to twelve (metrics, analytics, cards-service, skills-service, gates-service, chorus-domain as extras) and which has since been cut back to the seven.
Content: 28 principles served live (XP's values and Hemenway's permaculture principles, with Jeff's own readings), the practices that express them, 15 policies (the Stop-hook rules such as the response word cap and "English only"), the decisions (DEC-* and ADR-*), the four roles (Jeff, Wren, Silas, Kade — each a bundle of five hats), the skills (the /verbs: /pull, /cw, /demo, /card, /gate-*, /clearing …), the RCAs.
Ownership: Wren authors the normative layer and owns the roles domain; Silas owns the RCAs (Proving) and the model's coherence as OWL-DBA; the security graph and identity stay Silas's (authN) while authz and automation are Wren's.""" ;
    chorus:model """The 2026-05-14 audit (four subagents over chorus.ttl, the shapes, the doc catalog and the live graph) found the relationships were the least coherent layer: hasDomain declared twice with conflicting signatures, consumes overloaded into dependency duty, belongsTo used 30+ times but never defined, partOf a phantom, Decision and RCA not even OWL classes, and Loom's content types with zero shapes. That audit is what produced the Athena product model: Product and Domain both recursive via hasChild, hasDomain single-declared Product → Domain, consumes Product → Service, contains Domain → content, atStep for value-stream placement (Jeff, 2026-05-14: "this is literally the Athena product model — products, subproducts, domains — services is missing").
Content classes, one per domain, each with its shape: Principle (label, comment, ownedBy), Practice (+ expresses ≥1 Principle), Policy (+ enforcedBy ≥1 gate/hook), Decision (decisionType ∈ {DEC, ADR}, decidedOn), RCA (incident, rootCause, occurredOn), Role (roleType ∈ {Agent, Human}), Skill (composedOf ≥1 ∈ {claude-code, mcp, gate, hook}). Universal constraint: every content instance is the object of exactly one contains edge — no orphan principles, no orphan policies.
Today the principles and policies are served from the graph (/api/loom/principles, /api/loom/policies) with the policy → principle edge real (#4077); decisions still live largely as markdown (roles/wren/decisions.md) awaiting the Loom Decisions API (#2318).""" ;
    chorus:pagesAndFlow """/loom/principles.html — the 28 principles, live from the graph (also GET /api/athena/subdomains/loom-principles/principles); the same set is injected into every role's session boot under "Principles (live from graph)".
/loom/policies — the 15 Stop-hook and gate rules, each crediting its principle (#4077 fixed the edge name; before it all 14 were orphans).
The roles pages and the role tiles read the derived state (#4028). Decisions: the Gathering docs decisions page and DECISIONS.md in about/; Chorus search for DEC-NNN.
Skills: invoked as /<name> in the terminal (30+ SKILL.md definitions symlinked into ~/.claude/skills/); no catalog UI yet.
Flow: a principle is minted (chorus_principles_create) → practices and policies cite it → the hooks enforce the policies at PreToolUse / Stop (word cap, nudge trap, memory-first, canonical-write guard) → an RCA or a correction from Jeff proposes a change to the principle set → the loop closes at Shaping. Interaction patterns (direction / ideation / demo / triage / swat / gemba / clearing / story / reflection) are detected by Wren and emitted to the spine for Borg.""" ;
    chorus:apiSurface """GET /api/loom/principles — the live principle set (28; the boot-envelope source). GET /api/athena/subdomains/loom-principles/principles — the same by domain.
MCP: chorus_principles_list / _get / _create (CRUD); chorus_decisions_list / _get; chorus_register_feedback; chorus_pain_card / chorus_pain_rollup (the reactive-card signal); loom-gemba (live observation of a role).
GET /api/loom/policies — the policy rows with their principle; /api/loom-metrics (the flow metrics over the spine tail).
Generated at :3360: /domains/principles, /practices, /policies, /decisions, /roles, /skills, /rcas as their classes land under the Athena model.
Enforcement is the hooks: chorus-hooks (Rust, ~36 modules) at PreToolUse / PostToolUse / UserPromptSubmit / Stop — the policies are executable there, not just narrative.
Designed, not built: POST /athena/principle/invoke and /practice/invoke at a decision point (pass card + decision-point, get the principles / practices that apply); the Loom Decisions API (#2318, POST/PUT/DELETE for DEC/ADR).""" ;
    chorus:asIs """As stated in loom-subproduct-design.html (Wren, 2026-05-14, AS-IS coherence audit) and loom-service-design.html (2026-04-05), plus the 2026-09 landings — not re-measured on 2026-09-03:
Populated then: principles (27) and practices (40); policies, decisions, rcas, roles, skills were shells or not classes. Served now: 28 principles live and injected at boot; 15 policies each crediting its principle (#4077); the seven domains exactly Jeff's intent set; the four roles as seed instances (#3838) with state derived from the streams (#4028).
Still narrative: decisions (218+ DEC-* and ADRs) live in markdown with no structured API and no validation that a decision is enforced — DEC-107 was broken for weeks undetected. Skills are file-based, not queryable, no catalog UI. Gate false positives erode trust (the framework sequence addressed root causes). Two vocabularies (chorus: / fw:) and the full ontology/instances duplication the audit named are graph-wide, still open.
Nine interaction patterns detected and emitted; emission is by the PM, not a hook.""" ;
    chorus:toBe """Decisions in the graph: Decision as a class with its shape (decisionType, decidedOn), the Loom Decisions API (#2318), decisions.md retired as the store — every DEC/ADR cited by IRI.
Skills queryable: Skill instances with composedOf, a registry API and a catalog Jeff can browse; skill invocation validated.
RCAs modeled (Silas, Proving): incident, rootCause, occurredOn — the learning corpus that feeds candidate principles (the validators → Loom loop; recurring incoherence → a principle).
Invoke at the decision point: principle / practice invoke returning what applies to this card at this step, not a list dump.
Policies self-proving: every gate ships with a negative proof (#3734) and its refusal names its state; the interaction-pattern emit becomes a hook, not a habit.
Loom as template: the coherence audit shape (up-edge, one containment predicate, populated-or-marked-planned, real classes with shapes, one vocabulary) replicated across the other products.""" ;
    chorus:notInScope """The structural layer (Product / Domain / Service, recursive containment) — lifted out of this design into Athena in 2026-05 and owned there.
The two-vocabularies problem (chorus: / fw:) and the ontology/instances duplication — graph-wide, not the Loom slice.
The Clearing surfaces (chat, tiles) and the board — Clearing; Loom's service design of 2026-04 listed them as components before the products were separated.
Gate mechanics (werk-demo running the five gates) — Werk; Loom defines the rules the gates enforce.""" ;
    chorus:references """loom-subproduct-design.html — Wren, 2026-05-14: the first subproduct design; the AS-IS coherence audit (structure up and down, the OWL, the SHACL, six findings) + the TO-BE OWL/SHACL model (the Athena product model, seven content classes and shapes). The source of promise / structure / model / to-be here.
loom-service-design.html — Wren, 2026-04-05: the nine components (roles, clearing, interactions, briefs, cards, skills, decisions, practices, policy), deployed vs missing. The source of pages / API / as-is here.
loom-value-stream-design.html — the Shaping-step loop. chorus-reference-model.html — the closest earlier Loom definition. roles-service-design.html, roles-domain-evolution.html — the roles domain. skill-lifecycle.html — skills. INTERACTION_PATTERNS.md — the nine patterns.
/loom/principles.html; platform/api/src/sparql/seeds/permaculture-principles.rq (the principle system's source of truth). ADR-045 (a domain is an owl:Class). Cards: #4077 (policies credit principles; English only), #3838 (roles as seed instances), #4028 (derived role state), #2318 (Decisions API), #3734 (no gate without a negative proof), #2152 (decisions graphed).
Chorus · designing/docs/loom-subproduct-design.html · #4080 · Wren · 2026-09-03""" ;
